{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.22695","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.22695","prefix":"10.48550","suffix":"arxiv.2509.22695","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2509.22695","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"alternateIdentifiers":[{"alternateIdentifierType":"arXiv","alternateIdentifier":"2509.22695"}],"creators":[{"name":"Wang, Zhitao","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Zhitao","familyName":"Wang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Wang, Yanke","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yanke","familyName":"Wang","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Wen, Jiangtao","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Jiangtao","familyName":"Wen","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Horowitz, Roberto","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Roberto","familyName":"Horowitz","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"name":"Han, Yuxing","nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yuxing","familyName":"Han","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"ReSeFlow: Rectifying SE(3)-Equivariant Policy Learning Flows"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2025,"subjects":[{"lang":"en","subject":"Robotics (cs.RO)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"lang":"en","subject":"Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","schemeUri":"http://www.oecd.org/science/inno/38235147.pdf","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2025-09-20T06:32:36Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-09-30T00:01:04Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025-09","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2025","dateType":"Issued"}],"language":null,"types":{"ris":"GEN","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"article","schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceType":"Article","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"1","rightsList":[{"rights":"arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license","rightsUri":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Robotic manipulation in unstructured environments requires the generation of robust and long-horizon trajectory-level policy with conditions of perceptual observations and benefits from the advantages of SE(3)-equivariant diffusion models that are data-efficient. However, these models suffer from the inference time costs. Inspired by the inference efficiency of rectified flows, we introduce the rectification to the SE(3)-diffusion models and propose the ReSeFlow, i.e., Rectifying SE(3)-Equivariant Policy Learning Flows, providing fast, geodesic-consistent, least-computational policy generation. Crucially, both components employ SE(3)-equivariant networks to preserve rotational and translational symmetry, enabling robust generalization under rigid-body motions. With the verification on the simulated benchmarks, we find that the proposed ReSeFlow with only one inference step can achieve better performance with lower geodesic distance than the baseline methods, achieving up to a 48.5% error reduction on the painting task and a 21.9% reduction on the rotating triangle task compared to the baseline's 100-step inference. This method takes advantages of both SE(3) equivariance and rectified flow and puts it forward for the real-world application of generative policy learning models with the data and inference efficiency.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"This work was submitted to 2026 IEEE International Conference on Robotics \u0026amp; Automation","descriptionType":"Other"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.22695","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"citationsOverTime":[],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2025-09-30T03:29:27.000Z","registered":"2025-09-30T03:29:27.000Z","published":"2025","updated":"2025-09-30T03:29:27.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"arxiv","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2509.22695","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[]},"versionOf":{"data":[]}}}}